# EntityTable + EmptyState — Mandatory Pattern

Every table in `convision-front` must use `EntityTable`. Never build a custom table UI or use raw `<table>` elements.

Every `EntityTable` must declare **both** empty-state props:

```tsx
<EntityTable<MyItem>
  columns={columns}
  queryKeyBase="my-feature"
  fetcher={({ page, per_page, search }) => myService.getForTable({ page, per_page, search })}
  emptyStateNode={
    <EmptyState
      leadingIcon={SomeLucideIcon}
      accentColor="#8753ef"            // use role accent or domain colour
      title="Sin registros"
      description="No hay elementos para mostrar en este momento."
    />
  }
  filterEmptyStateNode={
    <EmptyState variant="table-filter" />
  }
/>
```

## Rules

- `emptyStateNode` — shown when there is **no data and no active search**. Use a domain-relevant icon (`lucide-react`) and a descriptive `accentColor`.
- `filterEmptyStateNode` — shown when a search/filter returns **zero results**. Always use `variant="table-filter"` (renders "Sin resultados" with a clear-filters button).
- Never omit either prop.
- Import from `@/components/ui/empty-state`.

## EmptyState quick-ref

| Variant | Icon | Title | When to use |
|---|---|---|---|
| `table-filter` | `Filter` | Sin resultados | Active search/filter returns nothing |
| `default` | none | Sin datos | Generic fallback only |
| custom | pass `leadingIcon` | custom | Domain-specific base state |

## Fetcher shape for EntityTable

The `fetcher` must return `{ data: T[], last_page: number, total: number }`.
Wrap the service call in a dedicated `getForTable` helper inside the service file when the raw API response has a different shape.
